# Drizzle ORM Rules

## Schema Location

- **Single source of truth**: `src/server/db/schema.ts`
- **Connection**: `src/server/db/index.ts`
- **Table prefix**: All tables use `eventifive_*` prefix

## Schema Best Practices

```typescript
// TEACHING: Always define relations for type-safe joins
// Relations don't create DB constraints, they enable Drizzle's relational queries
import { pgTable, text, timestamp, uuid } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";
import { relations } from "drizzle-orm";

export const event = pgTable("eventifive_event", {
  // TEACHING: uuid with defaultRandom() is better than serial for distributed systems
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  // TEACHING: Always use timestamp with timezone for proper date handling
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true }).defaultNow().notNull(),
  // TEACHING: Use text() for variable-length strings, varchar() only when you need length limits
  title: text("title").notNull(),
});

// TEACHING: Define relations separately - this enables .with() queries
export const eventRelations = relations(event, ({ many, one }) => ({
  submissions: many(submission),
  organizer: one(user, {
    fields: [event.organizerId],
    references: [user.id],
  }),
}));
```

## Query Patterns

```typescript
import { db } from "@/server/db";
import { event } from "@/server/db/schema";
import { eq, and, desc, sql } from "drizzle-orm";

// TEACHING: Simple select with WHERE clause
const events = await db.select().from(event).where(eq(event.organizerId, userId));

// TEACHING: Use .limit() and .offset() for pagination - never fetch all records
const paginatedEvents = await db
  .select()
  .from(event)
  .where(eq(event.isPublic, true))
  .orderBy(desc(event.createdAt))
  .limit(10)
  .offset(page * 10);

// TEACHING: Use transactions for multiple related operations
await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
  await tx.insert(event).values({ ... });
  await tx.insert(eventSettings).values({ ... });
  // If any fails, all are rolled back
});
```

## Migration Commands

- `pnpm db:push` - Quick development iteration (no migration files)
- `pnpm db:generate` - Generate migration files for production
- `pnpm db:migrate` - Run pending migrations
- `pnpm db:studio` - Visual database browser

## Common Pitfalls

1. **Never use raw SQL** unless absolutely necessary - lose type safety
2. **Always paginate** large result sets
3. **Use transactions** for related inserts/updates
4. **Index foreign keys** and frequently queried columns
5. **Never store sensitive data** without encryption

## Key Enums

```typescript
// Roles for RBAC (role-based access control)
export const rolesEnum = pgEnum("role", ["super_admin", "organizer", "user"]);

// Certificate roles
export const certificateRoleEnum = pgEnum("certificate_role", [
  "speaker", "committee", "reviewer", "facilitator"
]);

// Payment status flow: unpaid → pending → paid (or refunded)
export const paymentStatusEnum = pgEnum("payment_status", [
  "unpaid", "pending", "paid", "refunded"
]);

// Subscription billing periods
export const billingPeriodEnum = pgEnum("billing_period", ["monthly", "yearly"]);

// Subscription lifecycle: pending → active → cancelled/expired
export const subscriptionStatusEnum = pgEnum("subscription_status", [
  "pending", "active", "cancelled", "expired"
]);

// Speaker/reviewer invite status
export const eventSpeakerStatusEnum = pgEnum("event_speaker_status", [
  "pending", "accepted", "rejected"
]);

// Event types
export const eventTypeEnum = pgEnum("event_type", [
  "congress", "seminar", "workshop", "scientific_meeting", "conference", "symposium"
]);
```

## Invite System Tables

```typescript
// TEACHING: Invites use separate tables for speakers, reviewers, and committee
// Each has different constraints (speakers: max 1, reviewers: max 3, committee: unlimited)

// Speaker invitations (max 1 per event)
export const eventSpeakers = pgTable("event_speakers", {
  eventId: text("event_id").references(() => event.id),
  speakerId: text("speaker_id").references(() => user.id),
  status: eventSpeakerStatusEnum("status").default("pending"),
});

// Reviewer invitations (max 3 per event)
export const eventReviewers = pgTable("event_reviewers", {
  eventId: text("event_id").references(() => event.id),
  reviewerId: text("reviewer_id").references(() => user.id),
  status: eventSpeakerStatusEnum("status").default("pending"),
});

// Committee members (unlimited)
export const eventCommittee = pgTable("event_committee", {
  eventId: text("event_id").references(() => event.id),
  committeeId: text("committee_id").references(() => user.id),
});
```

## Calendar/Schedule Tables

```typescript
// TEACHING: Program sessions for event scheduling
export const programSession = pgTable("program_session", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  eventId: text("event_id").references(() => event.id),
  title: varchar("title", { length: 255 }),
  startTime: timestamp("start_time"),
  endTime: timestamp("end_time"),
  roomId: text("room_id").references(() => room.id),
});

export const room = pgTable("room", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  eventId: text("event_id").references(() => event.id),
  name: varchar("name", { length: 100 }),
  capacity: integer("capacity"),
});
```

